{%- comment -%}
  Works out the brush count, comparison price and saving for one variant. Shopify is the only source of prices.
  Outputs three numbers separated by "|": units | compare (cents) | saving (cents). 0 means "none".

  - units: the number at the start of the Bundle option value ("2 Brushes" = 2, "1 Brush" = 1; anything else = 1).
    Used only for the "2 grooming brushes" wording, never for any price.
  - compare: the variant's OWN Shopify compare_at_price, only when it is higher than its selling price.
    Nothing is calculated or invented: no compare-at on the variant means no strikethrough and no saving.
  - saving: compare_at_price minus price, both from the same variant.

  Accepts:
  - variant: variant object
  - label: the Bundle option value for this variant ("2 Brushes"); defaults to the variant title
{%- endcomment -%}
{%- liquid
  assign vp_label = label | default: variant.title
  assign vp_units = vp_label | replace: '-', ' ' | split: ' ' | first | plus: 0
  if vp_units < 1
    assign vp_units = 1
  endif
  assign vp_compare = 0
  assign vp_save = 0
  if settings.show_compare_at_price and variant.compare_at_price > variant.price
    assign vp_compare = variant.compare_at_price
    assign vp_save = vp_compare | minus: variant.price
  endif
  echo vp_units | append: '|' | append: vp_compare | append: '|' | append: vp_save
-%}
